DevOps Interview: Tricky Scenarios You’ll Get Stuck In (With Best Answers)

1️⃣ Production Server Is Down – What Will You Do?

❌ Where Candidates Get Stuck

●Panic

●Jump directly to restarting servers

●No clear troubleshooting order


✅ What Interviewer Wants

●Calm, structured incident handling

●Prioritization

●Communication mindset


⭐ Best Answer Format

1. Check monitoring alerts (CPU, memory, disk, network)
2. Identify scope (single service / entire system)
3. Check recent deployments or config changes
4. Check logs (application, system, load balancer)
5. Rollback if needed
6. Communicate status to stakeholders
7. Do post-incident RCA

🎯 Pro Tip Line

“I focus on restoring service first, then root cause.”


2️⃣ CI/CD Pipeline Fails Suddenly

❌ Where Candidates Get Stuck

●Saying “I’ll check logs” (too generic)

●Not mentioning recent changes


✅ What Interviewer Wants

●Debugging approach

●Understanding of pipeline stages


⭐ Best Answer Format

1. Identify which stage failed (build/test/deploy)
2. Check recent code or dependency changes
3. Verify credentials/secrets didn’t expire
4. Re-run pipeline with verbose logs
5. Fix and add validation to prevent recurrence

🎯 Smart Add-On

“I prefer small commits to isolate failures faster.”


3️⃣ Kubernetes Pod Is Not Starting

❌ Where Candidates Get Stuck

●Only saying: kubectl get pods

●Not knowing next steps


✅ What Interviewer Wants

●Hands-on kubectl knowledge

●K8s fundamentals

⭐ Best Answer Format

kubectl describe pod <pod>
kubectl logs <pod>
Check:
- Image pull errors
- CrashLoopBackOff
- Resource limits
- ConfigMaps / Secrets

🔥 Interview Gold Line

“Most pod issues are config, image, or resource related.”


4️⃣ Application Is Slow After Deployment

❌ Where Candidates Get Stuck

●Blaming the app team immediately

●No performance analysis steps


✅ What Interviewer Wants

●Observability knowledge

●Dev + Ops mindset

⭐ Best Answer Format

1. Compare metrics before and after deployment
2. Check CPU, memory, DB latency
3. Review application logs
4. Check autoscaling behavior
5. Rollback if SLA is impacted


5️⃣ Secrets Are Exposed in Git Repo

❌ Where Candidates Get Stuck

●Saying “I’ll delete the repo”

●Ignoring damage control


✅ What Interviewer Wants

●Security awareness

●Real-world response


⭐ Best Answer Format

1. Rotate exposed secrets immediately
2. Remove secrets from Git history
3. Use secret manager (Vault / AWS Secrets Manager)
4. Add pre-commit hooks
5. Educate team

🔐 Strong Line

> “Deleting the repo doesn’t fix leaked credentials.”
